    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="30">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 30</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete">⁊ lufige man Godes riht heonan forð georne wordes ⁊ dæda; þonne wurð us Godes miltse þe gearuwre.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="30" corresp="#wit-k">Ac lufige man Godes riht heonan forþ georne wordes ⁊ weorces; þonne wyrð þysse þeode sona God milde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">Ac lufige man Godes riht heonan forþ georne wordes and weorces; þonne wyrð þysse þeode sona God milde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">But God's law shall henceforth be zealously cherished in word and in deed; then God will forthwith be gracious towards this people.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">But God’s law is to be willingly embraced henceforth in word and deed; then will God immediately show mercy to this people.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Sondern man achte hinfort Gottes Gebot sorgsam in Wort und Werk (Thaten D); dann wird Gott alsbald diesem Volke gnädig werden (uns Gottes Gnade umso bereitwilliger D).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But let God's law be eagerly loved henceforth in word and work (deeds, D); then God will soon become merciful to this people (God's mercy will be all the readier for us, D).</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="255"><ref target="clause:VAtr_26">V Atr 26</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 26</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:ICn_19-3">I Cn 19.3</ref></note>
